An artifact carrying no `sessions:` key is not an error: a note names it on stderr, the run exits 0,
and the artifacts array comes back empty.

Contract note: the plan's I/O sketch expected such an artifact to appear in the array with a
`skipped` reason and empty `sessions` / `totals`. It does not — the entry is omitted entirely, and
`skipped` is reserved for the already-stamped case. This case pins the behaviour as shipped.

-- fixtures/cwd/vault/plan/index.md --
---
title: No sessions here
---

Body.
-- cmd --
booping session-stats vault/plan/index.md --dry-run
-- exit --
0
-- stdout --
{
  "artifacts": []
}
-- stderr --
note: no sessions: key in vault/plan/index.md; skipped
